From fc65e441e54ba05b2edafc5c227c457e81431a44 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Petr=20=C5=A0tetiar?= <petr.stetiar@prplfoundation.org>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 18:10:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Radio: keep MBSSID Advertisement off on a radio with hidden
 SSID VAPs
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

pWHM runs one global hostapd process for all radios. On the Wi-Fi 7 /
MLO QEMU (mac80211_hwsim) board the default config has a hidden
(SSIDAdvertisementEnabled=0) backhaul VAP on every radio (AP7/8/9) and
IEEE80211ax.MBSSIDAdvertisementMode is left at its default "Auto"
(odl/wld_radio.odl:3284). wld_rad_getMbssidAdsMode()
(src/wld_radio.c:3276-3296) resolves Auto to the highest driver
supported mode, on 6 GHz only; hwsim advertises 8 MBSSID interfaces
and EMA profile periodicity 3 (mac80211_hwsim.c:5335-5336, read by
s_parseMbssidAds(), src/nl80211/wld_nl80211_parser.c:1110-1150, and
turned into the On and Enhanced support bits by
src/Plugin/wifiGen_rad.c:319-324), so the 6 GHz radio (wlan0) resolves
to Enhanced and wld_hostapd_cfgFile_setRadioConfig()
(src/nl80211/wld_hostapd_cfgFile.c:594-600) writes "mbssid=2" into
wlan0's radio section, while s_setVapCommonConfig() (:927)
independently writes "ignore_broadcast_ssid=2" for the hidden backhaul
BSS of that same radio. Nothing in pWHM checks the combination.

Upstream hostapd rejects it: hostapd_config_check_bss()
(src/ap/ap_config.c:1516 in the deployed 2025 source, unchanged in
current hostap main: "full_config && bss->ignore_broadcast_ssid &&
conf->mbssid") fails the whole /tmp/wlan0_hapd.conf with "Hidden SSID
is not suppored when MBSSID is enabled", hostapd exits at startup,
wldDmn respawns it every 5 s and, as it is the one hostapd of all
three radios, every Radio stays Down and every AccessPoint Disabled
from the moment the hidden VAP is enabled together with the others
(109-pwhm-power-save.t, "Enable all AccessPoints"). The same board
config works on Freedom only because its QCA hostapd fork implements
hidden non-transmitted MBSSID profiles and has no such check; OpenWrt's
own hostapd writers do not work around the upstream check either, so
any pWHM build against an upstream hostapd is exposed.

Fix: resolve the effective MBSSID Advertisement mode to Off when any
VAP configured on the radio is hidden. The check is placed in
wld_rad_getMbssidAdsMode() itself (the standards/requested/supported
resolution is kept verbatim as s_getReqMbssidAdsMode()) rather than in
the config writer only, so that every consumer of the decision agrees:
the radio section writer (no "mbssid" / "mbssid_max"), the per-BSS
"mbssid_index" (wld_hostapd_cfgFile.c:906), the config main VAP
selection (wld_rad_hostapd_getCfgMainVap(),
src/nl80211/wld_rad_hostapd_api.c:701-714), the BSS inclusion rule
(wld_hostapd_ap_needWpaCtrlIface(),
src/nl80211/wld_hostapd_ap_api.c:1639-1650) and the FSM's non-Tx BSS
disable path (src/Plugin/wifiGen_fsm.c:599). All configured VAPs are
considered, not only the enabled ones: the config main VAP is written
with start_disabled=1 when it is disabled and hostapd's check does not
exempt it, and an enabled-only rule would flip the radio's "mbssid"
under a running hostapd on every enable/disable of a hidden VAP, where
the warm "ADD bss_config" of the hidden BSS would then trip the very
same hostapd check. The requested mode and the reported capability
(suppMbssidAdsModes) are left as they are, and the requested SSID
visibility is preserved: no BSS is unhidden or dropped. The writer
logs one NOTICE per radio config generation when the fallback is in
effect (new wld_rad_isMbssidAdsBlockedByHiddenVap()).

Runtime: toggling SSIDAdvertisementEnabled on a radio whose VAPs were
all visible (or back) changes the radio level "mbssid", which a running
hostapd only takes from a (re)start; per-BSS SET commands can not apply
it. The decision is taken at radio level, in the FSM dependency phase
(s_checkRadDependency(), src/Plugin/wifiGen_fsm.c): whenever the config
file is about to be rewritten (GEN_FSM_MOD_HOSTAPD) while hostapd is
alive and no start is scheduled already, the radio "mbssid" of the
saved config file and of a freshly generated config are compared (new
wld_hostapd_cfgFile_isRadMbssidChanged(), absent means 0) and, when
they differ, SECDMN_ACTION_OK_NEED_RESTART is requested once for the
radio: the existing path that stops hostapd, drops the pending warm
actions and starts it again with the rewritten config. Deciding there
instead of in the per-BSS wld_ap_hostapd_setNoSecParams() path makes it
independent of the changed VAP having a ready wpactrl connection: a
disabled VAP is omitted from the config under MLO or MBSSID
(wld_hostapd_ap_needWpaCtrlIface()) and has none, so a visibility
change on it, like the creation or deletion of a hidden VAP, would
otherwise rewrite the saved config with the new mode without a restart,
after which no comparison could see the running mode any more. The
per-BSS readiness gate of the SET operations (s_doSyncAp()) is
unchanged.

The fallback is unconditional: a hostapd that does implement hidden
non-transmitted MBSSID profiles (the QCA fork) also loses MBSSID/EMA on
a radio with a hidden VAP. Gating it on an explicit backend capability
is left for a follow-up.

Not specific to hwsim: any pWHM build against upstream hostapd with a
hidden VAP on a radio where MBSSID Advertisement resolves to On or
Enhanced hits the same crash loop.

Signed-off-by: Petr Štetiar <petr.stetiar@prplfoundation.org>
---
 include/wld/wld_hostapd_cfgFile.h |  1 +
 include/wld/wld_radio.h           |  1 +
 src/Plugin/wifiGen_fsm.c          | 16 +++++++++++
 src/nl80211/wld_hostapd_cfgFile.c | 42 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 src/wld_radio.c                   | 44 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 5 files changed, 103 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/include/wld/wld_hostapd_cfgFile.h b/include/wld/wld_hostapd_cfgFile.h
index 45fcfea664be..ff6fd968390f 100644
--- a/include/wld/wld_hostapd_cfgFile.h
+++ b/include/wld/wld_hostapd_cfgFile.h
@@ -69,6 +69,7 @@
 
 void wld_hostapd_cfgFile_create(T_Radio* pRad, char* cfgFileName);
 void wld_hostapd_cfgFile_createExt(T_Radio* pRad);
+bool wld_hostapd_cfgFile_isRadMbssidChanged(T_Radio* pRad);
 bool wld_hostapd_cfgFile_update(char* configPath, const char* interface, const char* key, const char* value);
 void wld_hostapd_cfgFile_setRadioConfig(T_Radio* pRad, swl_mapChar_t* radConfigMap);
 void wld_hostapd_cfgFile_setVapConfig(T_AccessPoint* pAP, swl_mapChar_t* vapConfigMap, swl_mapChar_t* multiAPConfig);
diff --git a/include/wld/wld_radio.h b/include/wld/wld_radio.h
index a90a7d58bd34..3d844ecabefa 100644
--- a/include/wld/wld_radio.h
+++ b/include/wld/wld_radio.h
@@ -154,6 +154,7 @@ T_AccessPoint* wld_rad_getFirstEnabledVap(T_Radio* pR);
 uint32_t wld_rad_countEnabledVaps(T_Radio* pR);
 wld_mbssidAdvertisement_mode_e wld_rad_getMbssidAdsMode(T_Radio* pRad);
 bool wld_rad_hasMbssidAds(T_Radio* pRad);
+bool wld_rad_isMbssidAdsBlockedByHiddenVap(T_Radio* pRad);
 
 T_AccessPoint* wld_rad_getVapByIndex(T_Radio* pRad, int index);
 T_EndPoint* wld_rad_getEpByIndex(T_Radio* pRad, int index);
diff --git a/src/Plugin/wifiGen_fsm.c b/src/Plugin/wifiGen_fsm.c
index 5be409170660..3d9278035fae 100644
--- a/src/Plugin/wifiGen_fsm.c
+++ b/src/Plugin/wifiGen_fsm.c
@@ -2254,6 +2254,22 @@ static void s_checkRadDependency(T_Radio* pRad) {
             s_clearRadDynConfActions(pRad);
         }
     }
+    /*
+     * The radio level "mbssid" follows the VAPs' SSID visibility
+     * (wld_rad_getMbssidAdsMode()) and can not be applied to a running hostapd
+     * with per-BSS SET commands: when the config file about to be written
+     * changes it, restart hostapd with the new config. Decided here, before
+     * any per-BSS action and before the config file is written, so that it
+     * does not depend on the changed VAP having a ready wpactrl connection
+     * (disabled VAPs are omitted from the config under MLO/MBSSID) and also
+     * covers VAP creation and deletion.
+     */
+    if(isBitSetLongArray(pRad->fsmRad.FSM_AC_BitActionArray, FSM_BW, GEN_FSM_MOD_HOSTAPD) &&
+       !isBitSetLongArray(pRad->fsmRad.FSM_AC_BitActionArray, FSM_BW, GEN_FSM_START_HOSTAPD) &&
+       wifiGen_hapd_isAlive(pRad) && wld_hostapd_cfgFile_isRadMbssidChanged(pRad)) {
+        SAH_TRACEZ_WARNING(ME, "%s: radio mbssid changed: need hostapd restart", pRad->Name);
+        s_schedNextAction(SECDMN_ACTION_OK_NEED_RESTART, NULL, pRad);
+    }
 }
 
 wld_fsmMngr_action_t actions[GEN_FSM_MAX] = {
diff --git a/src/nl80211/wld_hostapd_cfgFile.c b/src/nl80211/wld_hostapd_cfgFile.c
index 94659967e9de..cc709cb853a2 100644
--- a/src/nl80211/wld_hostapd_cfgFile.c
+++ b/src/nl80211/wld_hostapd_cfgFile.c
@@ -597,6 +597,8 @@ void wld_hostapd_cfgFile_setRadioConfig(T_Radio* pRad, swl_mapChar_t* radConfigM
         SAH_TRACEZ_INFO(ME, "%s: Setting MBSSID Advertisement %d", pRad->Name, mbssidAdsMode);
         swl_mapCharFmt_addValInt32(radConfigMap, "mbssid", (mbssidAdsMode == MBSSID_ADVERTISEMENT_MODE_ENHANCED) ? 2 : 1);
         wld_secDmn_addToMapSuppCfgParamValueInt32(pRad->hostapd, radConfigMap, "mbssid_max", amxc_llist_size(&pRad->llAP));
+    } else if(wld_rad_isMbssidAdsBlockedByHiddenVap(pRad)) {
+        SAH_TRACEZ_NOTICE(ME, "%s: MBSSID Advertisement kept off: hidden SSID VAP(s) configured, hostapd rejects hidden BSSes with mbssid", pRad->Name);
     }
 
     pRad->pFA->mfn_wrad_updateConfigMap(pRad, radConfigMap);
@@ -1493,6 +1495,46 @@ void wld_hostapd_cfgFile_createExt(T_Radio* pRad) {
     wld_hostapd_cfgFile_create(pRad, pRad->hostapd->cfgFile);
 }
 
+/**
+ * @brief check whether the radio level "mbssid" of the hostapd config file
+ * would change if the config file was written now
+ *
+ * The effective MBSSID Advertisement mode follows the VAPs' SSID visibility
+ * (wld_rad_getMbssidAdsMode()) and is written in the radio section of the
+ * config file, which a running hostapd only takes from a (re)start.
+ * The comparison only needs the saved config file and the datamodel, not a
+ * wpactrl connection to any BSS, so it also covers VAPs omitted from the
+ * config (disabled VAPs under MLO/MBSSID) and VAP creation/deletion.
+ *
+ * @param pRad radio context
+ *
+ * @return true when a saved config file exists and its radio level "mbssid"
+ *         (absent means 0) differs from the one of the freshly generated config
+ */
+bool wld_hostapd_cfgFile_isRadMbssidChanged(T_Radio* pRad) {
+    ASSERTS_NOT_NULL(pRad, false, ME, "NULL");
+    ASSERTS_NOT_NULL(pRad->hostapd, false, ME, "NULL");
+    wld_hostapd_config_t* pSavedCfg = NULL;
+    ASSERTI_TRUE(wld_hostapd_loadConfig(&pSavedCfg, pRad->hostapd->cfgFile), false, ME, "%s: no saved config", pRad->Name);
+    wld_hostapd_config_t* pNewCfg = NULL;
+    bool changed = false;
+    if(wld_hostapd_createConfig(&pNewCfg, pRad)) {
+        const char* savedMbssid = wld_hostapd_getConfigParamValStr(pSavedCfg, NULL, "mbssid");
+        const char* newMbssid = wld_hostapd_getConfigParamValStr(pNewCfg, NULL, "mbssid");
+        savedMbssid = swl_str_isEmpty(savedMbssid) ? "0" : savedMbssid;
+        newMbssid = swl_str_isEmpty(newMbssid) ? "0" : newMbssid;
+        changed = !swl_str_matches(savedMbssid, newMbssid);
+        if(changed) {
+            SAH_TRACEZ_WARNING(ME, "%s: radio mbssid changed (%s -> %s)", pRad->Name, savedMbssid, newMbssid);
+        }
+    } else {
+        SAH_TRACEZ_ERROR(ME, "%s: fail to generate new config", pRad->Name);
+    }
+    wld_hostapd_deleteConfig(pNewCfg);
+    wld_hostapd_deleteConfig(pSavedCfg);
+    return changed;
+}
+
 /**
  * @brief update a configuration file for the hostapd
  *
diff --git a/src/wld_radio.c b/src/wld_radio.c
index c13da2cc776f..e08c170b2a6a 100644
--- a/src/wld_radio.c
+++ b/src/wld_radio.c
@@ -3273,7 +3273,12 @@ uint32_t wld_rad_countEnabledVaps(T_Radio* pR) {
     return count;
 }
 
-wld_mbssidAdvertisement_mode_e wld_rad_getMbssidAdsMode(T_Radio* pRad) {
+/*
+ * MBSSID Advertisement mode resolved from the radio's standards, the
+ * requested mode and the driver's supported modes, i.e. the mode the radio
+ * would use if the hostapd config allowed it.
+ */
+static wld_mbssidAdvertisement_mode_e s_getReqMbssidAdsMode(T_Radio* pRad) {
     wld_mbssidAdvertisement_mode_e mode = MBSSID_ADVERTISEMENT_MODE_OFF;
     ASSERTS_NOT_NULL(pRad, mode, ME, "NULL");
     swl_radioStandard_m stds = pRad->supportedStandards;
@@ -3295,6 +3300,43 @@ wld_mbssidAdvertisement_mode_e wld_rad_getMbssidAdsMode(T_Radio* pRad) {
     return mode;
 }
 
+/*
+ * true when any VAP configured on the radio has SSID broadcasting disabled,
+ * i.e. would be written to hostapd as a hidden BSS (ignore_broadcast_ssid != 0).
+ * All configured VAPs are considered (not only the enabled ones): the config
+ * main VAP is written with start_disabled=1 when disabled, and hostapd's
+ * config check does not exempt it.
+ */
+static bool s_hasHiddenVap(T_Radio* pRad) {
+    T_AccessPoint* pAP = NULL;
+    wld_rad_forEachAp(pAP, pRad) {
+        if(!pAP->SSIDAdvertisementEnabled) {
+            return true;
+        }
+    }
+    return false;
+}
+
+bool wld_rad_isMbssidAdsBlockedByHiddenVap(T_Radio* pRad) {
+    ASSERTS_NOT_NULL(pRad, false, ME, "NULL");
+    return ((s_getReqMbssidAdsMode(pRad) != MBSSID_ADVERTISEMENT_MODE_OFF) && s_hasHiddenVap(pRad));
+}
+
+wld_mbssidAdvertisement_mode_e wld_rad_getMbssidAdsMode(T_Radio* pRad) {
+    wld_mbssidAdvertisement_mode_e mode = s_getReqMbssidAdsMode(pRad);
+    /*
+     * hostapd (hostapd_config_check_bss()) rejects the whole radio config when
+     * any of its BSSes is hidden while mbssid is enabled: keep MBSSID
+     * Advertisement off on a radio with hidden VAP(s), whatever the requested
+     * and supported modes, so that the effective mode is the same for the
+     * config writer, the BSS selection and the main VAP selection.
+     */
+    if((mode != MBSSID_ADVERTISEMENT_MODE_OFF) && s_hasHiddenVap(pRad)) {
+        mode = MBSSID_ADVERTISEMENT_MODE_OFF;
+    }
+    return mode;
+}
+
 bool wld_rad_hasMbssidAds(T_Radio* pRad) {
     return (wld_rad_getMbssidAdsMode(pRad) != MBSSID_ADVERTISEMENT_MODE_OFF);
 }
